# Atlaris Architecture Relationships

Use this map to navigate service ownership, import direction, and high-risk boundaries before editing. Prefer the named feature boundaries and request wrappers over reaching into core modules directly.

## Layer Map

```mermaid
flowchart TB
  App["src/app\nroutes, RSC, server actions, API handlers"]
  UI["src/components + src/hooks\nclient UI and orchestration"]
  Features["src/features\ndomain services, workflows, adapters"]
  Lib["src/lib\ninfra, auth, API wrappers, DB queries, logging, proxy"]
  Shared["src/shared\nleaf types, schemas, constants"]
  Supabase["supabase\nschema, RLS, migrations, runtime, service-role"]

  App --> UI
  App --> Features
  App --> Lib
  UI --> Features
  UI --> Lib
  Features --> Lib
  Features --> Shared
  Lib --> Shared
  Lib --> Supabase
  Features --> Supabase

  Features -. forbidden .-> App
  Shared -. forbidden .-> Features
```

## Request And Data Flow

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  Proxy["src/proxy.ts\nClerk middleware, CSP,\nmaintenance, workflow gate"]
  Policy["src/lib/proxy/middleware-policy.ts"]
  Boundary["src/lib/api/request-boundary.ts\nroute / component / action"]
  Auth["src/lib/api/auth.ts\nClerk auth + app user"]
  Context["src/lib/api/context.ts\nrequest context"]
  Runtime["supabase/runtime.ts\nRLS DB runtime"]
  RLS["supabase/rls.ts\nRLS context factory"]
  Route["src/app/**\nroute/action/component"]
  Feature["src/features/**\nfeature boundary/service"]
  Queries["src/lib/db/queries/*\nDrizzle query modules"]
  Schema["supabase/schema + migrations"]

  Proxy --> Policy
  Proxy --> Route
  Route --> Boundary
  Boundary --> Auth
  Boundary --> Feature
  Auth --> Context
  Context --> Runtime
  Runtime --> RLS
  Feature --> Queries
  Queries --> Runtime
  Runtime --> Schema
```

## Key Relationship Edges

- `src/proxy.ts` --> `src/lib/proxy/middleware-policy.ts`: ingress policy, CSP, maintenance, workflow callback gating.
- `src/app/**` --> `src/lib/api/request-boundary.ts`: wrap API routes, RSC loaders, and server actions with `requestBoundary.route`, `.component`, or `.action`.
- `requestBoundary.*` --> `src/lib/api/auth.ts`: establish Clerk auth and ensure the internal app user before RLS work.
- `src/lib/api/auth.ts` --> `src/lib/api/context.ts`: creates request context used by RLS-aware DB access.
- `src/lib/api/context.ts` --> `supabase/runtime.ts` --> `supabase/rls.ts`: DB runtime and RLS context wiring.
- `src/app/(app|marketing|auth)` --> `src/components`, `src/hooks`, `src/features`: route groups compose UI and feature boundaries.
- Client islands --> `src/app/_shared/client-api.ts`: use typed client API helpers for browser calls.
- Plan UI/SSE hooks --> `src/app/api/v1/plans/stream`: generation session entrypoint.
- `/api/v1/plans/stream` --> `src/features/plans/session/plan-generation-session.ts`: session orchestration behind `requestBoundary.route`.
- `PlanGenerationSession` --> `PlanLifecycleService`: plan lifecycle is the central hexagonal service.
- `PlanLifecycleService` --> collaborator ports declared in `src/features/plans/lifecycle/service.ts` (persistence, quota, generation, finalization) and `creation-pipeline.ts` (`CreationGatePorts`): depends on ports, not concrete adapters.
- `src/features/plans/lifecycle/factory.ts` --> `plan-persistence-store.ts`, `generation.ts`, `generation-finalization/store.ts`, billing tier/duration policy: concrete lifecycle wiring on one DB client.
- `src/features/plans/lifecycle/generation.ts` --> `src/features/ai/orchestrator.ts`: model/provider orchestration.
- `AI orchestrator` --> `src/features/ai/providers/` factory/OpenRouter/router/mock: provider selection and invocation spans.
- `generation-finalization/store.ts` --> DB modules/tasks/attempts/usage: persist completed plan state and metering effects.
- App/UI plan reads --> `src/features/plans/read-projection/service.ts`: read plan projections through this feature boundary.
- `src/features/plans/read-projection/service.ts` --> `src/lib/db/queries/plans.ts`: allowed raw plan-query access point.
- Generation work (lesson content, plan regeneration) --> `src/features/billing/*-quota-boundary.ts`: quota checks and reservations enter through feature-owned boundaries.
- Billing quota boundaries --> `src/features/billing/metered-reservation.ts` + `metered-quota-boundary-core.ts`: core reservation logic; do not call directly from routes.
- Clerk billing webhook (`src/app/api/v1/clerk/billing/webhook`) + maintenance reconcile (`src/app/api/internal/maintenance/billing/reconcile-clerk`) --> `src/features/billing/clerk-billing/` (plan-mapping, projection, reconciliation): Clerk Billing subscription state.
- Billing reads (subscription route, plans page, settings billing) --> `src/features/billing/account-snapshot.ts`: account tier/usage snapshot boundary.
- Lesson generation route (`.../lesson-content/generate/handler.ts`) --> `src/features/lesson-content/start-module-lesson-generation-workflow.ts`: choose async workflow or inline path.
- Lesson generation work --> `src/features/lesson-content/run-module-lesson-generation-work.ts`: module lesson generation orchestrator.
- Lesson content work --> lesson quota boundary + OpenRouter + service-role persistence: generation, metering, and privileged writes.
- Internal worker routes --> `src/lib/api/internal/internal-worker-access.ts` (jobs) and `src/lib/api/internal/maintenance-route.ts` (maintenance): authenticate internal jobs before execution.
- Internal worker routes --> `src/features/jobs/**`: job execution and regeneration orchestration.
- Email notifications --> `src/features/notifications/email/` (delivery workflow, Resend adapter, service-role persistence via `src/lib/db/queries/email-*.ts`); entered from `src/app/api/v1/notifications` and `src/app/api/internal/maintenance/notifications`.
- Telemetry entrypoints --> `src/instrumentation.ts`, `sentry.*.config.ts`, `src/lib/logging/request-context.ts`, `src/lib/observability/metrics.ts`: tracing, request logs, metrics, AI invocation spans.

## Boundary Rules

- `src/features/**` must not import `src/app/**`; features are reusable domain boundaries below routes.
- `src/shared/**` stays leaf-only: shared contracts, types, schemas, and constants should not import `src/features/**`.
- `src/app/**` must not import blocked raw plan read query exports from `src/lib/db/queries/plans.ts`; use `src/features/plans/read-projection/service.ts`.
- Use `requestBoundary.route`, `.component`, or `.action` before auth, RLS-sensitive DB work, or feature mutations from app entrypoints.
- RLS-sensitive queries in high-risk modules must receive an explicit DB client; avoid hidden global DB access.
- `@supabase/service-role` is allowed only in named feature, workflow, or worker boundaries; Oxlint blocks it from `src/app/**`, `src/lib/api/**`, and `src/lib/integrations/**`.
- Billing consumers should enter through quota boundaries, `account-snapshot.ts`, or `clerk-billing/` modules, not `metered-reservation.ts` or `metered-quota-boundary-core.ts` directly.
- Plan lifecycle code should depend on lifecycle ports and factory-wired adapters, not concrete persistence/provider modules from the service core.
- Drizzle query modules live in `src/lib/db/queries/*`; schema, RLS, and migrations live under `supabase/`.

